# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT ADD TRAILING-SLASH RULES. THEY CAUSE A REDIRECT LOOP.
#
# It is tempting to add rules like:
#
#     /about                  /about/                 301!      # <-- BREAKS
#
# on the reasoning that netlify.toml sets pretty_urls = false and therefore
# bare /about will not reach /about/. That reasoning is wrong twice over:
#
#   1. pretty_urls only controls whether ".html" is stripped from URLs. It
#      does not switch off the asset server's own directory handling, so
#      Netlify already serves /about correctly with no rule at all.
#   2. Netlify IGNORES the trailing slash when matching a _redirects source,
#      so the source "/about" matches /about/ too. The rule then redirects
#      /about/ to itself, and the "!" forces it even though /about/index.html
#      exists. The page becomes an infinite loop.
#
# This was added and reverted on 10/18/2026. It took out /about/, /contact/,
# /book-online/, /iv-therapy/, /hormone-replacement-therapy/ and
# /peptide-therapy/ — six of the ten pages — and the only reason it was
# caught is that every rule was fetch-tested on staging instead of being
# assumed to work. Test the rules, not just the file.
#
# The same hazard applies to any rule whose source and destination differ
# only by a trailing slash. The cross-page rules above are safe because
# source and destination are genuinely different paths.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

